  "fixture": "Public environment/path/UUID/time/version/receipt vectors only. Fresh real JVM negative tests. OPS uses fixed fake Java and local static unit syntax verification; no host manager/service/credential changes. FLOCK uses isolated retained regular files, real libc and util-linux2.41.3 with narrow native fault ports. No host lockfile, UID or service mutation.",
  "oracle": "051/PT221..232: bounded nonsecret canonical input, missing/null/unknown rejection, no parsing diagnostics, exact ASCII receipt after owned resource closure, 0/10/50/70 mapping, unexpected runtime escape/fixed fatal message, native admission negatives,64 independent invocations. 018/PT001..008: fixed receipt byte matrix and JVM exit override; all base directives and4 selected previous-key profiles; actual sh/ShellCheck/systemd-analyze with recorded outputs; release classpath/JDBC runtime/Java25 flags. 003/PT-OPS-FLOCK-001..008: independent flock exit20 while Java holds and Java empty while external holds; fcntl does not conflict; one of32 wins; retained original inode remains locked after path replacement; errno11 alone is contention; fixed open flags0x80000/flock6, close once and IO diagnostic redaction. 005/PT-OPS-LOCK-001..008: MaintenanceFileLock connects held directories/inode and real flock, requires euid0, root:root0755 directories, root:root0600 empty single-link file, RW tmpfs/access ACL absent, same device and re-open identity before/after callback. All native open/close positions and attributes/FS/ACL faults, null/runtime failure,32 simultaneous requests, no repair and fixed3 boot-only tmpfiles entries are checked. 007/PT-OPS-STOP-001..016: independent ASCII seven-property vectors, exact loaded/inactive/dead/no Job/zero PID admission; missing/duplicate/unknown/control/1024+1/null rejection; fixed API then Web fresh reads; interrupts preserved and64 concurrent invocations; fixed systemctl argv/5-second wait/1025-byte read; all three stdio close failures crossed with normal/exit/timeout/oversize/read/interrupt; child-only TERM and no force kill; empty inherited environment replaced with exact five nonsecret variables; actual unprovisioned host not-found states rejected. 009/PT-OPS-ENV-001..004: SS343 independent two-line ASCII golden; every byte changed to each other possible byte, missing/extra/duplicate/quoted/CRLF/unknown-key input, all128 UUID bit changes and +/-1 microsecond fail exact run binding; years0001/9999, null, caller-owned fresh arrays and64 concurrent results are independently checked. 011/PT-OPS-CFG-001..006: fixed static DB/version two-line ASCII grammar before Map parsing; literal rendered template, port1/65535 and database1/63, version1/16 and unique list65535/65536, wrong source/duplicate/unknown/alias/quotes/controls/high-byte/oversize/null rejection, fixed redaction and64 concurrent checks. Independent SS values, no production-generated expected. 013/PT-OPS-EFILE-001..008: real retained inode/channel reads with synthetic root/GID/local-FS metadata; exact source and run bytes, metadata types/modes/owner/group/link/size/device/ACL/FS before IO, max+1 bounded EOF and size/identity/time rechecks, same-name replacement rejection, explicit nine-key null/type matrix, every IO/owned-close occurrence, compound raw IO diagnostics stripped,64 reads and start/mid/final interrupts preserved. No source-derived expected or reflection into private production state.",
  "limitations": "Java coverage belongs to launcher, not a shell percentage. Parent OS flock/inactive/backup/run binding, root-owned environment validation/publication, actual unit credential provisioning and timeout/TERM behavior, full batch, NK CHR and IT/ST are NOT certified. LinuxFileLock is a low-level capability only; root/type/UID/ACL/stable-namespace admission and parent lifecycle are not supplied by it. CLOEXEC is asserted at the native call boundary, not an actual inherited-FD inspection; aarch64 ABI selection only, execution is amd64. MaintenanceFileLock PT uses synthetic root UID/GID/tmpfs admission over real isolated unprivileged files. Actual root/tmpfiles provisioning and parent inactive/backup/DB handoff remain unverified. STOP is read-only transient state observation, not service stopping or a lease. Deployed units, root execution, parent restart prohibition/cgroup validation and integration remain unverified. Trusted fixed systemctl/OS assumptions apply; timeout is tested using a process fault port, not a real stalled manager or TERM-ignoring descendant. Run EnvironmentFile codec neither reads/writes files nor chooses the authoritative run. Root ownership/ACL/NOFOLLOW/bounded read/atomic publication, static setting file validation, OS lifecycle and durable run anchorSSC055 remain unverified. Static source bytes are now certified separately; bounded retained-inode IO, root metadata, atomic publication and parent-child lifecycle remain pending. EFILE certifies borrowed-root read only. Fixed ancestor namespace/account resolution, OS lock continuity, source stability until systemd reads, atomic publisher and actual root deployment remain caller responsibilities.",
